The walk rate is the whole argument. Ingle has drawn 83 walks against 105 strikeouts at AAA this season across 455 plate appearances, an 18% clip that translates to 14.2% at the MLB level against an MLB average of 8.5%. That discipline is why his .419 OBP plays, and the .232 ISO at AAA suggests real gap-to-gap pop even if the translation shaves it to .175. The ceiling here is a platoon or bench catcher whose on-base ability keeps him useful; the floor is a depth option whose value collapses if pitchers can tighten the zone and he can't adjust, because the K% isn't clean enough to carry him on contact alone.

